{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets","id":429582,"title":"Auspice Renown and Facets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-05T18:48:51-08:00","id":429582,"title":"Auspice Renown and Facets","content":"If I invest in my Auspice Renown, do I only get an increase of my Moon Gift, or do I also get both the next Moon Gift Facet and a Shadow or Wolf Gift Facet of the appropriate Renown as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T18:55:08-08:00","id":429603,"title":"","content":"The book says that whenever you get a renown increase you can unlock that facet in a shadow gift you possess, doesn't make mention of it being exlusive with the moon gift increase, so I'd say yes, one advantage having an auspice incurs for the Forsaken that the Pure don't get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T20:20:55-08:00","id":429691,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I'm having a serious problem trying to figure out Gifts. (I think the game could have really used a character creation example). So I have a player creating an Ithaeur Iron Master weapon smith. He has Wisdom 1, Cunning 1 and Purity 1. He chooses Elemental and Shaping gifts. which would grant him the following:<br /> <br /> Crescent Moon 1<br /> and then can choose 2 facets from either of the two shadow gifts and 1 facet from any of the 3 Wolf Gifts. these facets do NOT have to align directly with the werewolf's renown (by that I mean he can have 3 wisdom facets if he wants). <br /> <br /> Am I understanding this correctly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T20:26:43-08:00","id":429696,"title":"","content":"the character gets crescent moon one, one facet from elemental, one facet from shaping and a wolf gift facet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T21:14:30-08:00","id":429793,"title":"","content":"That doesn't sound right.<br /> <br /> Page 99:<br /> &quot;Each time your character increases her auspice Renown, she unlocks a Facet of her Moon Gift. Every time she increases a different Renown, she gains a Facet of a Shadow or Wolf Gift.&quot;<br /> <br /> When you raise your auspice renown, it seems like it <b>must</b> go into your Moon Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T21:23:09-08:00","id":429802,"title":"","content":"&quot;Unlocking a Shadow Gift costs 5 Experiences, or 3 if it<br /> is favored by auspice or tribe. Once it is acquired, the Uratha<br /> gains a single Facet within that Gift immediately. She may then<br /> freely purchase additional Facets for 2 Experiences each at any<br /> time she wishes. One limitation applies: she may never unlock<br /> a Facet associated with a Renown in which she possesses no<br /> dots. Every time the Uratha gains a new dot of any Renown,<br /> she may unlock the respective Renown Facet in a Gift that she<br /> possesses at no cost. This spiritual development causes the Gift\u2019s<br /> marks to squirm and cut their way deeper into the Uratha\u2019s<br /> being, opening up the fresh Essence flows of the new Facets.<br /> If the werewolf has already unlocked all the Facets associated<br /> with that Renown in the Gifts she possesses, the free unlock<br /> is stored until she gains a new Gift with a suitable Facet.&quot;<br /> <br /> Page 115<br /> <br /> Going by that it seems that my interpretation was correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> And I headed back to the development blog, but Stew also did write this: <br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Renown gives a free Facet of a Gift that the character knows as before \u2014 and Auspice Renown grants a Shadow Gift in addition to a Moon Gift.&quot; </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":991,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","user":"pgolasze13","date":". 03-06-2015, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T21:45:19-08:00","id":429818,"title":"","content":"This sounds more like a contradiction than a misinterpretation, both bits are pretty straight forward.<br /> <br /> &quot;Each time your character increases her auspice Renown, she unlocks a Facet of her Moon Gift.&quot; Each character at this time only has 1 Moon Gift so until they potentially add more to each auspice (referenced on page 85) this only leaves one option.<br /> <br /> &quot;Every time she increases a <u>different</u> Renown, she gains a Facet of a Shadow or Wolf Gift.&quot; The key word here is different.<br /> <br /> &quot;Every time the Uratha gains a new dot of any Renown, she may unlock the respective Renown Facet in a Gift that she possesses at no cost.&quot; Pretty straight forward, but conflicts directly with the wording in the renown section earlier in the book.<br /> <br /> One of these two is going to need rewording.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=429802#post429802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I headed back to the development blog, but Stew also did write this:<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Renown gives a free Facet of a Gift that the character knows as before \u2014 and Auspice Renown grants a Shadow Gift in addition to a Moon Gift.&quot; </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah well now we know which section is going to need rewording.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T21:51:29-08:00","id":429820,"title":"","content":"Okay, thanks guys, I guess my &quot;problem&quot; stems from the fact that the game follows different rules at Character Creation than it does later. ie: at character creation your Auspice Renown grants you 1 gift while later it grants two. <br /> <br /> I'm guessing they didn't want to front load a new wolf too heavily. *shrug* Now I have to explain to my other player that her 1e character has to reallocate a dot of Wisdom renown. (she began at 3) <br /> <br /> Thanks again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T22:42:09-08:00","id":429854,"title":"","content":"I wrote up a big explanation based on my own reading at rpgNET: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?711826-WtF-Idigam-Chronicle-Second-Edition-What-do-we-know-It-s-out!&amp;p=18798878#post18798878\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...8#post18798878</a><br /> <br /> Copy-and-pasting...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">GENERAL RULE: You may never acquire a Facet if you have 0 dots in that Renown. Contrapositive: If you have 1+ dots in a Renown, you may acquire a Facet of that Renown. These sentences are equivalent and true. I've marked all the cases where this is relevant with a *.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">CHARGEN</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Auspice Renown 1: Moon Gift 1. Pick a Wolf Gift Facet*.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Auspice Renown 2: Moon Gift 2.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Combine Affinity Lists from Auspice and Tribe. Pick two.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gain one Facet* in each.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">DURING PLAY</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Unlock a Moon Gift at any time for 5 Experiences. Purchase Facets in any Moon Gift for 2 Experiences. Only relevant when more Moon Gifts are published.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Unlock a Shadow Gift after Siskur-Dah upon a relevant spirit. This costs 5 Experiences. If the Gift is in your Auspice or Tribe affinity list, it costs 3 Experiences. Immediately gain a Facet*.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Purchase Facets* in any unlocked Shadow Gift for 2 Experiences.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Purchase any Wolf Gift Facet* at any time for 1 Experience.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Upon gaining Auspice Renown, (a) receive a Moon Gift Facet for free and (b) receive a Shadow Gift Facet of that Renown for free.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Upon gaining non-Auspice Renown, receive a Shadow Gift Facet of that Renown for free.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Freebie Facets are never wasted; if you don't have an eligible Shadow Gift, bank the freebie until you do.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">RITES</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Learn two 1-dot Rites or one 2-dot Rite at chargen. Purchase during play for 1 Experience per dot after being taught.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":2758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","user":"Errol216","date":".  removed question about Auspice Renown 3 as it's actually not possible 03-06-2015, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T23:02:13-08:00","id":429887,"title":"","content":"It specifically says that one cannot start with a renown at three (so a Elodoth Iminir will still have to pick something other than Honor for his third Renown) so, yeah, 2 is probably out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T23:11:54-08:00","id":429892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=429820#post429820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, thanks guys, I guess my &amp;quot;problem&amp;quot; stems from the fact that the game follows different rules at Character Creation than it does later. ie: at character creation your Auspice Renown grants you 1 gift while later it grants two. <br /> <br /> I'm guessing they didn't want to front load a new wolf too heavily. *shrug* Now I have to explain to my other player that her 1e character has to reallocate a dot of Wisdom renown. (she began at 3) <br /> <br /> Thanks again.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a deliberate choice after play testing to deal with a problem identified around how Facet choice extrapolated out long term. I can't recall exactly what the issue was at the moment, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T00:30:34-08:00","id":429933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=429887#post429887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It specifically says that one cannot start with a renown at three (so a Elodoth Iminir will still have to pick something other than Honor for his third Renown) so, yeah, 2 is probably out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, dammit. This is why I caveat posts like this with how bad my reading ability is. Going to edit my previous post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T03:13:06-08:00","id":429970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=429854#post429854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Upon gaining Auspice Renown, (a) receive a Moon Gift Facet for free and (b) receive a Shadow Gift Facet of that Renown for free.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Upon gaining non-Auspice Renown, receive a Shadow Gift Facet of that Renown for free.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Freebie Facets are never wasted; if you don't have an eligible Shadow Gift, bank the freebie until you do.</span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Errol has the right of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T05:52:38-08:00","id":430112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=429892#post429892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a deliberate choice after play testing to deal with a problem identified around how Facet choice extrapolated out long term. I can't recall exactly what the issue was at the moment, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I figured as much. I didn't mean to come off as complaining. I get the reason for decisions like that, it was just causing &quot;static&quot; in my brain before it was explained outright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T05:58:34-08:00","id":430131,"title":"","content":"I don't get why starting with Renown 2 in your Auspice Renown cheats you out of a free facet... The min/maxer bug at the back back of my brain just refuses to die no matter how much I try to squash it! I'll be forever that one free facet short! lol...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:24:30-08:00","id":430172,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'll probably allow it in my games, we don't usually care about an extra power here or there and I think that the fact that if you go too over the top with your exploits you make it harder to outdo themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:10:14-08:00","id":430229,"title":"","content":"That's kind of weird, yeah, regarding the second dot of Auspice Renown screwing you out of a free Shadow Gift Facet at Chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:27:43-08:00","id":430244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430131#post430131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get why starting with Renown 2 in your Auspice Renown cheats you out of a free facet... The min/maxer bug at the back back of my brain just refuses to die no matter how much I try to squash it! I'll be forever that one free facet short! lol...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 84, 'If she has two dots in her auspice\u2019s Renown, she gains the second-dot Facet of that Moon Gift. Otherwise, she gains a facet of a Wolf Gift.' Providing you're not a Ghost Wolf, you end up with the same amount of gifts. 1 Moon, 2 Shadow, and 1 Wolf. Or 2 Moon, 2 Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-06-2015, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:43:35-08:00","id":430267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430244#post430244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Page 84, 'If she has two dots in her auspice\u2019s Renown, she gains the second-dot Facet of that Moon Gift. Otherwise, she gains a facet of a Wolf Gift.' Providing you're not a Ghost Wolf, you end up with the same amount of gifts. 1 Moon, 2 Shadow, and 1 Wolf. Or 2 Moon, 2 Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I think the point is, if you take a second Auspice Renown there.. you won't get a Shadow Gift for that Renown. Just a Moon gift, whereas if you buy it up in-game, you get both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:44:44-08:00","id":430269,"title":"","content":"I think what we're referring to is that if, at chargen, you buy your second dot in your Auspice Renown at 2, you get 1 Moon Gift Facet and 1 Shadow/Wolf Gift Facet for the first dot, but only the second Moon Gift Facet for the second dot, with no complimentary Shadow/Wolf Gift Facet as if you had bought it after chargen.<br /> <br /> Or am I still reading it wrong? That entire section needs two or three <b>clear</b> examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:51:25-08:00","id":430275,"title":"","content":"I think this is clarified on page 99:<br /> <br /> &quot;Each time your character increases her<br /> auspice Renown, she unlocks a Facet of her Moon Gift. Every<br /> time she increases a different Renown, she gains a Facet of a<br /> Shadow or Wolf Gift.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thus, chargen and spending experiences work the same. Renown increases only ever give you one free facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:57:05-08:00","id":430279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430275#post430275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is clarified on page 99:<br /> <br /> &quot;Each time your character increases her<br /> auspice Renown, she unlocks a Facet of her Moon Gift. Every<br /> time she increases a different Renown, she gains a Facet of a<br /> Shadow or Wolf Gift.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thus, chargen and spending experiences work the same. Renown increases only ever give you one free facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, on page 115 it says this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Every time the Uratha gains a new dot of any Renown,<br /> she may unlock the respective Renown Facet in a Gift that she<br /> possesses at no cost. This spiritual development causes the Gift\u2019s<br /> marks to squirm and cut their way deeper into the Uratha\u2019s<br /> being, opening up the fresh Essence flows of the new Facets.<br /> If the werewolf has already unlocked all the Facets associated<br /> with that Renown in the Gifts she possesses, the free unlock<br /> is stored until she gains a new Gift with a suitable Facet.&quot;<br /> <br /> It doesn't neccessarily go against what you said, but it makes it unclear, after all, it does say &quot;Every time&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: Additionally, reading it as you did, it'd mean that an Uratha could never get his Auspice facets by raising renown, since that was taken by his Moon Gift instead, thus giving them LESS affinity with facets of that Renown than more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":585,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","user":"Seidmadr","date":".  Insight. 03-06-2015, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:03:17-08:00","id":430285,"title":"","content":"I do agree that the phrasing on page 115 and 85 are unclear. They should be rephrased to be consistent with page 99. Honestly, it would make more sense to me that page 99 should be the definitive rule and the other two references should just be removed. There is no reason to state the same rule three times in the book. Page 85 should just talk about experience costs and page 115 should speak to the experience of getting a gift without going into the mechanics or cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:06:38-08:00","id":430287,"title":"","content":"Currently, after character creation, whenever you raise your Auspice Renown you get both the new dot in your Moon Gift and you also get a Facet of that Renown unlocked in a Shadow Gift you possess.<br /> <br /> That's how it's supposed to work, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:24:17-08:00","id":430301,"title":"","content":"It's pretty expensive to break into new Shadow gifts, the same cost in experiences as a Primal Urge. But the other facets are kind of cheap. The bigger buy in is probably better, I noticed in our Blood and Smoke game characters were advancing a lot faster. And while that's a nice step from first edition, at points it did seem a little too fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:43:53-08:00","id":430338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430287#post430287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, after character creation, whenever you raise your Auspice Renown you get both the new dot in your Moon Gift and you also get a Facet of that Renown unlocked in a Shadow Gift you possess.<br /> <br /> That's how it's supposed to work, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is there a design reason why at chargen this is different? Or is it a oversight/mistake on the chargen wording?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:47:38-08:00","id":430340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430131#post430131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get why starting with Renown 2 in your Auspice Renown cheats you out of a free facet... The min/maxer bug at the back back of my brain just refuses to die no matter how much I try to squash it! I'll be forever that one free facet short! lol...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely a permanent -1 XP for people who make that choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 03-06-2015, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T09:01:39-08:00","id":430357,"title":"","content":"It doesn't cheat you-you either end your initial selection of four gifts with either a Wolf Facet or a Moon Facet.<br /> <br /> I mean, it literally goes Moon, Shadow, Shadow, Wolf/Moon(If Auspice Renown is 2) by the way it's described in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T09:08:14-08:00","id":430380,"title":"","content":"Yeah. But you get cheated out of one facet, over-all. If you increase that Renown in-game, you get two Facets, if you do it during chargen, you get one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T09:08:23-08:00","id":430381,"title":"","content":"Huh. According to p99, my statement about gaining non-Auspice Renown is incorrect, since you have a choice between Wolf Gift Facet or Shadow Gift Facet. And the part on p99 about gaining Auspice Renown is definitely contradictory with p114/115. =/<br /> <br /> My current understanding is that an Auspice Renown gets you 2 Facets (Moon and Shadow), whereas non-Auspice gets you 1 Facet (Shadow or Wolf). This contradicts eberg's statement on post 21 about Renown only ever giving 1 Facet. I feel like the correct interpretation is actually &quot;Renown -&gt; 1 Facet (Shadow or Wolf); if Auspice, then +1 Facet (Moon)&quot;, which <i>no one</i> has actually said.<br /> <br /> Definitely agree that the rules for gaining Facets during play only need to be in one place. The bit about &quot;(including during character creation)&quot; on p115 especially needs to go away; the chargen rules are reasonably clear on their own: it's just stuff like that line that gets in their way. I think it needs to be explicitly stated somewhere that, if you have 1+ dots in a Renown, then you can purchase or freely acquire a Facet of that Renown on any Gift, whether you're unlocking it or already have it.<br /> <br /> ...incidentally, where do I post typos I find? I haven't been recording them, but I do keep finding little issues. (Also, there's a layout issue on page 204 where the Red Minister image covers about 4 words of the Funnel-Web's description.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T09:30:12-08:00","id":430385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430380#post430380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. But you get cheated out of one facet, over-all. If you increase that Renown in-game, you get two Facets, if you do it during chargen, you get one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a renown you're not paying for, and assumedly you're also increasing your power decently across the board. Seems a fair trade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:25:18-08:00","id":430398,"title":"","content":"Here's the way I plan to rule:<br /> Gaining a dot in any Renown gives you 1 facet of the appropriate type in a Shadow Gift you know, or any Wolf Gift. If that Renown is also your Auspice renown, you also get the next facet of your Moon Gift.<br /> <br /> At character creation, you gain 3 dots of Renown. One of those must be your Auspice renown, and one of them must not be. Each of these renown gains follow the normal rules for gaining Renown. If you do not take two dots of your Auspice Renown, you gain a Facet in a Wolf Gift. So your options are:<br /> <br /> 1 primary, 2 non primary; gives you 1 Moon Facet, 3 Shadow or Wolf Facets, and 1 Wolf Facet<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> 2 primary, 1 non-primary; gives you 2 Moon Facets and 3 Shadow or Wolf Facets.<br /> <br /> That way character creation follows the same rules as normal experience buys, you don't &quot;lose&quot; any facets either way, and you end up with a total of 5 facets at character creation either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:26:41-08:00","id":430399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430385#post430385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a renown you're not paying for, and assumedly you're also increasing your power decently across the board. Seems a fair trade.</div> </div> </div> </div>The werewolf who starts with Auspice 2, Non Auspice 1 <b>has fewer facets</b> than the werewolf who starts with Auspice 1, Non Auspice 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:28:45-08:00","id":430400,"title":"","content":"Would ghost wolves get an extra wolf facet under that system? At the moment they lose one by RAW anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-06-2015, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:36:00-08:00","id":430404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430385#post430385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a renown you're not paying for, and assumedly you're also increasing your power decently across the board. Seems a fair trade.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get 3 Renown at chargen if you get them spaced out in 3 different Renowns you get: <br /> <br /> 1 Moon + 2 Shadow + 1 Wolf<br /> <br /> On your first Auspice Renown exp buy you get <br /> <br /> 1 Moon + 1 Shadow/Wolf<br /> <br /> So you are now at AuspRen 2 and 2 other Renowns at 1 and you have 6 facets<br /> <br /> If you go 2 Ausp Ren 1 other Renown at chargen you get:<br /> <br /> 2 Moon + 2 Shadow<br /> <br /> On your first Renown buy to equal the other character you get<br /> <br /> 1 Shadow/Wolf<br /> <br /> So you are now 2 AuspRen and 2 other Renowns at 1 and you have 5 facets<br /> <br /> So you are missing one. I\u00b4m not saying its a big deal, and can be easily house ruled. Its just that while I\u00b4m not a munchkin (as in buying all the right abilities), I do kinda obsess over choice returns performance.<br /> <br /> Anyways, some people understand and others don\u00b4t, but the facts are clear that choosing a same Renown Tribe/Auspice (like classical Bone/Ithaeur) is a underperforming choice at post chargen Renown/Facets comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:49:23-08:00","id":430413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430400#post430400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would ghost wolves get an extra wolf facet under that system? At the moment they lose one by RAW anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost wolves are screwed to another level, as they don\u00b4t get Tribe Renown ( 3 exp ) or the 3 Tribe Gifts ( 15 exp!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T11:07:17-08:00","id":430448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430400#post430400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would ghost wolves get an extra wolf facet under that system? At the moment they lose one by RAW anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, cause they would only have 2 renown gains. Their only option is<br /> <br /> 1 primary, 1 non-primary; gives 1 Moon Facets, 2 Shadow or Wolf Facets, and 1 Wolf Facet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-06-2015, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T11:48:06-08:00","id":430475,"title":"","content":"I was about to post something asking where you people were getting a third dot at character creation, but then rolled a Success on my Intelligence + Academics roll to <i>read</i>.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that is... a tad annoying. You're getting a tax on doubling up and starting with the second Facet of your Moon Gift.<br /> <br /> That's gonna bug me. Part of me is saying that the players who double up should have a &quot;free&quot; unlock that they have to sit on for a session or two. Maybe they get the first time they finish a Sacred Hunt?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> My line of thinking is that that would maintain parity with spending experience; I'll just point out that they start with one Facet <i>less</i> than they should have prior to the Sacred Hunt, and that starting out without doubling up and buying a dot in their Auspice Renown in play would give them the exact same number of facets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 03-06-2015, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T11:56:12-08:00","id":430477,"title":"","content":"For real though, just increasing the number of starting Shadow Facets to 3 solves the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:03:52-08:00","id":430641,"title":"","content":"This could really use some clarity on the character generation side of things. I asked this hoping for clarification and I'm just more confused.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's not confusion, and just me thinking 'but, it doesn't make sense that Character Generation would have this disparity compared to purchasing it after character generation, so obviously readings that create that disparity don't make sense' even if I know intellectually that the writers intended for it to be there. I guess I kinda get it, but I don't like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 03-06-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:26:16-08:00","id":430674,"title":"","content":"Okay, new point of clarity: I am not particularly concerned about game balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:32:39-08:00","id":430703,"title":"","content":"Well - unless I am wrong - effectively, the extra facet that a 1,1,1 renown selector gets at Chargen is a wolf facet - that is, 1 xp. This has a direct parallel with Vampire 2e, where if a starting vampire begins with one of his discipline dots in a non-affinity discipline or a blood sorcery, he effectively gets a 1xp discount. It aint no hill a beans.<br /> <br /> I did find it confusing too: stating more clearly that you get the moon facet plus a shadow facet for each affinity renown would help; or better, a little sepia-inked chart. But on the other hand - wow - the synergy, brutality and visceral wolfiness of these new gifts is superb. I don't get the complaints about power level; having run through a few scenarios, they hunt like no other (go go insight and knowledge gifts!) and the new Nature Glory facet is killer. The tone of the lot of them is synergistic and really mean at isolating prey when they are vulnerable, working them to where they are exposed, and then eating them. Gritty kudos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:33:15-08:00","id":430704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430674#post430674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, new point of clarity: I am not particularly concerned about game balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted. On this particular point (character generation vs normal progression) I am particularly concerned with game balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:28:13-08:00","id":430766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430641#post430641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This could really use some clarity on the character generation side of things. I asked this hoping for clarification and I'm just more confused.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's not confusion, and just me thinking 'but, it doesn't make sense that Character Generation would have this disparity compared to purchasing it after character generation, so obviously readings that create that disparity don't make sense' even if I know intellectually that the writers intended for it to be there. I guess I kinda get it, but I don't like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is EXACTLY where my confusion came from earlier. I finally wrapped my mind around it and feel much better now... I do have to say though that this thread is causing me to go cross-eyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T02:38:56-08:00","id":431154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=430477#post430477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For real though, just increasing the number of starting Shadow Facets to 3 solves the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it doesn't solve anything if you don't condition an extra shadow/wolf to the 2nd Auspice Renown, like when exp buying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T09:30:17-08:00","id":431269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431154#post431154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it doesn't solve anything if you don't condition an extra shadow/wolf to the 2nd Auspice Renown, like when exp buying.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what increasing the number of starting Shadow Facets <i>does</i>. You'd get a dot of Primary Renown from your Auspice, which gives you a Moon Facet and a Shadow/Wolf Facet for free. A dot of your Tribe's Renown from your tribe, which gives you a Shadow/Wolf Facet, plus a Moon Facet if it also happens to be your Primary Renown type. Then you get a 3rd Renown dot of your choice (keeping in mind the limit of 2 in your Primary Renown at character creation), which gives you a Shadow/Wolf Facet and a Moon Facet if it happens to also be your Primary Renown type. Then if you still only have one Moon Facet you get a free Wolf Facet. That's a total of 2 Moon, 3 Shadow/Wolf, or 1 moon, 1 Wolf, 3 Shadow/Wolf. As opposed to the current 2 Moon, 2 Shadow/Wolf or 1 Moon, 1 Wolf, 2 Shadow/Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-07-2015, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:18:19-08:00","id":431530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431269#post431269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a total of 2 Moon, 3 Shadow/Wolf, or 1 moon, 1 Wolf, 3 Shadow/Wolf. As opposed to the current 2 Moon, 2 Shadow/Wolf or 1 Moon, 1 Wolf, 2 Shadow/Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately that does not solve the problem of getting a free Wolf out of the deal if you avoid starting with a second dot of auspice renown.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:38:45-08:00","id":431578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431530#post431530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately that does not solve the problem of getting a free Wolf out of the deal if you avoid starting with a second dot of auspice renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but what's a single 1xp Wolf Facet? Similarly, a vampire ends up 1xp ahead if they spend one of their free starting Discipline dots on an out of clan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:47:11-08:00","id":431586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431578#post431578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but what's a single 1xp Wolf Facet?</div> </div> </div> </div>About one or two weeks, depending on your beat income.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431578#post431578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, a vampire ends up 1xp ahead if they spend one of their free starting Discipline dots on an out of clan</div> </div> </div> </div>Two wrongs don't make a right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T11:47:52-08:00","id":431588,"title":"","content":"The point is to start with the right number of free gifts for the renown dots whilst keeping the number of gifts total the same regardless of what tribe/auspice combo you pick. Yeah, you get a free wolf gift if you don't double up, but it evens out once you start actually buying dots with experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:01:37-08:00","id":431602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431588#post431588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you get a free wolf gift if you don't double up, but it evens out once you start actually buying dots with experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>You get a free wolf gift even if you double up, as long as it is non auspice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:04:43-08:00","id":431607,"title":"","content":"No you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:09:10-08:00","id":431610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431586#post431586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About one or two weeks, depending on your beat income.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it takes the guy who started with the free Wolf Gift 3-6 weeks to get the second Facet in their Moon Gift. By that logic, you actually come out 2-4 weeks <i>ahead</i> if you double up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431586#post431586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two wrongs don't make a right.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would the alternative be? Let the player who doubles up on Auspice Renown have one Facet more than the one who doesn't? The experience levels would be balanced, but the characters' actual capabilities would not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:15:21-08:00","id":431616,"title":"","content":"I think it works. You basically just pick 3 renown dots, then the facets they come with as if you were earning them in play, and then when you're done count them and if n&lt;5 throw in a wolf gift too. Can't say fairer than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:41:26-08:00","id":431660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431616#post431616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it works. You basically just pick 3 renown dots, then the facets they come with as if you were earning them in play, and then when you're done count them and if n&lt;5 throw in a wolf gift too. Can't say fairer than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I'm advocating. Although I would keep the 2 dot maximum on starting Auspice Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:55:51-08:00","id":431678,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that was my attempt to spell your idea out in my own words. I think three shadow gifts also lets us go the two affinity / one not route requiem allows you go with disciplines. Gives a bit more wiggle room at chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:06:48-08:00","id":431689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431607#post431607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just double checked, and it is definitely possible for a character to start with 2 dots of Non Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431610#post431610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but it takes the guy who started with the free Wolf Gift 3-6 weeks to get the second Facet in their Moon Gift. By that logic, you actually come out 2-4 weeks <i>ahead</i> if you double up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can be pretty variable. It might be a huge bonus if that Moon Facet perfectly suits your build. Or it might be rather dubious. Meanwhile the Wolf Facet is almost always going to be high value because you get to pick whichever one fits your character best. You also have another dot of renown somewhere else that is either boosting non auspice renown based abilities you apparently favor over boosts to your auspice renown, or giving you more facet options by being a third dot of renown. There is also the rather weak point that it is probably easier to justify gaining auspice renown than non auspice renown for the average werewolf character.<br /> <br /> Not really another point, but just food for thought. A pretty decent number of werewolf games do not let you buy renown with XP. It is awarded for deeds during play.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431610#post431610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would the alternative be? Let the player who doubles up on Auspice Renown have one Facet more than the one who doesn't? The experience levels would be balanced, but the characters' actual capabilities would not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrrm. Hrrm. I don't really have a good alternative!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T13:34:07-08:00","id":431714,"title":"","content":"You don't get two facets with a dot of non-auspice renown though. that's where the issue lies. You want double tribal, knock yourself out. Doesn't do shit to the gift tally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-07-2015, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T16:41:07-08:00","id":431996,"title":"","content":"Nowhere in the book does it clearly state that you get both a Moon Gift facet and a Shadow Gift facet when you gain a point of Auspice Reknown. In two places (pg 85, pg 115), what happens when you get Auspice Renown is ambiguous and could be read that way, but in the remaining place (pg 99), it is stated clearly that you gain a Moon facet when your Auspice Renown goes up and you get a Shadow or a Wolf facet when a non-Auspice Renown increases. This is consistent with how character generation works: if you get a second point in your Auspice Renown, you get a Moon facet instead of a Wolf facet. In deference to Chris' work on the book, I really don't think his assertion that the other interpretation is what was intended holds up.<br /> <br /> Really, it would be helpful if Stew weighed in, since he's the one that stitched the book together. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:38:47-08:00","id":432035,"title":"","content":"He confirmed you get both all the way back in the comments of the Gifts preview. We also have one of the writers in this thread confirming that's the way it's supposed to work. Also, logically if you didn't get both, you wouldn't be able to get Shadow or Wolf Facets in your primary Renown without buying them individually, which would be weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:39:20-08:00","id":432036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=431996#post431996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere in the book does it clearly state that you get both a Moon Gift facet and a Shadow Gift facet when you gain a point of Auspice Reknown. In two places (pg 85, pg 115), what happens when you get Auspice Renown is ambiguous and could be read that way, but in the remaining place (pg 99), it is stated clearly that you gain a Moon facet when your Auspice Renown goes up and you get a Shadow or a Wolf facet when a non-Auspice Renown increases. This is consistent with how character generation works: if you get a second point in your Auspice Renown, you get a Moon facet instead of a Wolf facet. In deference to Chris' work on the book, I really don't think his assertion that the other interpretation is what was intended holds up.<br /> <br /> Really, it would be helpful if Stew weighed in, since he's the one that stitched the book together. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It should be fairly clear from 114 and 115 that you gain both a Shadow facet and a Moon Facet at the same time when you raise Auspice Renown. I can assure you that this was what was intended at the time of writing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On page 114, I wrote that, for Moon Gifts, 'Whenever the Uratha gains a dot in her auspice Renown (including during character creation) she gains the Facet of equal dot rating to her new Renown total.' Ie, let's say a Cahalith, raise your Glory to from 2 to 3 and you get your third dot in Gibbous Moon.<br /> <br /> On page 115, talking about Shadow Gifts, I wrote that 'Every time the Uratha gains a new dot of any Renown, she may unlock the respective Renown Facet in a Gift that she possesses at no cost.' As noted, this is referring to Shadow Gifts, and it also references Renown Facets (you'll note that Facets in Shadow Gifts are denoted by their Renowns; Facets in Moon Gifts are not). So, our Cahalith raises Glory from 2 to 3 and hence gains a Glory Renown Facet in one of the Shadow Gifts you have unlocked.<br /> <br /> Both of these unlocks occur because the Renown in question is the Cahalith's Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> The addition of the Wolf Facet to character creation for characters who don't go for their Auspice Renown starting at 2 was implemented for a different reason.<br /> <br /> If the actual intent changed such that you only get the Shadow Facet unlock with non-Auspice Renown then that was a change that occurred very late in the day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T07:25:33-07:00","id":458044,"title":"","content":"This thread has been linked a few times recently, so I figure I should bump it, and maybe sumaraize my reading. Chris has done a good job sumarizing one of the main points, but didn't discuss another strong line of contention in the thread:<br /> <br /> Point 1: Everyone starts with 4 Facets. This includes Ghost Wolves, people with an Auspice Renown at 2, and people with an Auspice Renown of 1. You can house-rule that everyone starts with more than that, but giving everyone the same number of Facets to start with means that people are generally at the same power level.<br /> <br /> Point 2: When buying Renown with XP, EVERY Renown increase grants a free Shadow or Wolf Facet in that Renown. If you already have all of the Facets of that type (which will only ever happen if you bought more Facets from one Renown at chargen than you did dots of that Renown - everyone starts with 5 Gifts open) then the next time you Open a Gift by running Siskur-Dah for it, you get two Facets for it.<br /> <br /> Point 3: If the Renown dot you got in-game happened to be your Auspice Renown, you ALSO get the corresponding Moon Gift Facet. Thus if your Ithaeur bought dot 3 of Wisdom, they could open BOTH Impossible Spoor (Wolf Gift of the Hunt - Wisdom) AND Shadow Hunter (Crescent Moon Gifts - 3 dots). Anyone else who wanted a Wisdom dot and Impossible Spoor could buy them together, but would not get anything else out of the deal.<br /> <br /> Point 4, which was already addressed in Point 1: if you think hash it out, this means that someone buying Renown and Facets in-game will be shorted by one Facet if they take two dots of their Auspice Renown at chargen. Too bad. Auspice is an unbalaning element and this particular aspect was balanced in another direction (towards making starter characters equal rather than down-the-road characters equal).<br /> <br /> Point 5: If you don't like it, fix it with house rules. One of the most vocal moderators on this thread says his group is happy to fix this by saying everyone gets 5 Facets at character generation. Talk to your gaming group. Come to a consensus. Really the only rule that matters is what makes your group's game flow well. The rest of them are in place to give everyone a common ground to start from.<br /> Just know here that the ramifications to makeing people with 2-Renown to start have an extra gift makes them extra powerful at first. Making them have the same number as everyone else means that they'll be about one session behind down the road. That said, Ghost Wolves will probably end up being 3-30 sessions behind on progression, depending on what road they take...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T11:50:35-07:00","id":458213,"title":"","content":"Nicely summarized, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T08:13:32-07:00","id":460018,"title":"","content":"I think a simple yet inorganic solution is that the werewolf that begins with 2 dots of auspice renown has a free facet stored as if he had already have all the facets of that renown bought.<br /> <br /> The the player can learn the facet at another time. My first thought would be to buy it when one player, half of the player or all the other players have bought their second dot of auspice renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2245-quimeradc","name":"Quimeradc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T10:54:33-07:00","id":460181,"title":"","content":"All of what you said is true and good, Quimeradc.<br /> My group ended up deciding that the fairness of Renown granting all the Facets it's supposed to outweighed the fairness of everyone starting with the same number of gifts. Thus, everyone got two Shadow Gifts and one Wolf Gift and however many dots of Moon Gift as they had Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> Then again, only one of four players didn't take their second Auspice dot, so your half condition was already met.<br /> <br /> I think the best point is that the book says one thing and there were reasons for it. Thereafter, it becomes a question of what the people you're playing with can agree on. If that's something other than what the book says, that's fine. If there's not agreement outside what the book says, the book is a good and well thought out default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}